# Font sizes

Set `font-size` only with a variable from `src/styles/fonts.css`. Do not write a px, rem, or em font size in CSS, inline styles, or canvas text.

Allowed sizes:

- `--ft-type-hero`
- `--ft-type-page`
- `--ft-type-title`
- `--ft-type-section`
- `--ft-type-card`
- `--ft-type-lead`
- `--ft-type-body`
- `--ft-type-ui`
- `--ft-type-secondary`
- `--ft-type-label`
- `--ft-type-caption`
- `--ft-type-micro`

Font families are `--ft-font` and `--ft-font-brand`. Leading and tracking that already exist are `--ft-leading-tight`, `--ft-leading-body`, and `--ft-tracking-tight`.

Pick the nearest existing step. Do not add a new size token unless the user asks to change `fonts.css`.

```css
/* BAD */
font-size: 14px;
font: 600 13px/1.2 var(--ft-font);

/* GOOD */
font-size: var(--ft-type-secondary);
font: 600 var(--ft-type-label)/1.2 var(--ft-font);
```
